      "writtenOn": "2023-03-16T21:42:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could, but already now 26 of the 32 bits are defined with meanings relating to the JEDEC \"serial flash protocol\", used by EEPROM and flash chips.  So I would almost say that if we in the future need more flags or parameters unrelated to serial flash, then another 32-bit argument could be appropriate.",
